<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-8587] High Contention in GridToStringBuilder.toStringImpl  </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8587</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;org.apache.ignite.internal.util.tostring.GridToStringBuilder#classCache implemented as&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ordinal HashMap with all operations syncronised by one&#160;ReadWriteLock.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;this can trigger high contention as this class widely used in toString() methods.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For instance it shoots when DEBUG or TRACE logs are&#160; enabled as count of toString() invocations increases in this case extremely.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We need to use ConcurrentHashMap instead and avoid global locks.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
